{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex","id":778610,"title":"Fallen vs. Pentex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-02T14:57:03-08:00","id":778610,"title":"Fallen vs. Pentex","content":"Pentex is entrenched and has a ton of resources and allies to draw upon. The Fallen can turn ordinary people into the extrordinary and can do just about anything with enough Faith. If the Fallen wanted to take over Pentex or create a new corporate empire to knock Pentex off of its perch, which would win?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:15:35-08:00","id":778627,"title":"","content":"Ah another one of your lovely hypothetical scenarios, so why do the fallen care about pentex? How do they even know about it since there isn't a listed pentex hq located anywhere in any of the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:47:34-08:00","id":778647,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Fallen know due to Lore of Patterns. And by &quot;Fallen&quot; I mean one of the factions of the Fallen. The Faustians, for instance, are scrounging to put together resources. This will inevitably mean competing with the other things out there and also working to stop humans from destroying each other. Eventually, as the Fallen try to create an international empire they can draw on and direct the nations with, they will find themselves having to fight to take their place at the top and prevent more destruction of the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:07:36-08:00","id":778666,"title":"","content":"Right so, a seemingly unrelated group of multinational corporations who serve an extra dimensional entity with aims of total world destruction are some how going to be found out and stopped by a group of fallen angels who through good vibes and hugs have also formed a &quot;empire&quot; with out tipping their hand to their own enemies or rivals not to mention the very race they created. <br /> <br /> Not to mention some how avoiding the ire of an entire species of shape shifting religious zealots who would view their existence as anathema to creation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T18:08:52-08:00","id":778723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=778666#post778666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right so, a seemingly unrelated group of multinational corporations <b>who serve an extra dimensional entity with aims of total world destruction</b> are some how going to be found out and stopped by a group of fallen angels who through good vibes and hugs have also formed a &quot;empire&quot; with out tipping their hand to their own enemies or rivals not to mention the very race they created.<br /> <br /> Not to mention some how avoiding the ire of an entire species of shape shifting religious zealots who would view their existence as anathema to creation...</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't actually serve that head. They serve the one that just wants to keep things squalid and miserable with bloated plutocrats on top. To that end, their &quot;service&quot; is very loose and pretty much just a bunch of normal skeevy business.practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T18:45:04-08:00","id":778739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=778666#post778666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right so, a seemingly unrelated group of multinational corporations who serve an extra dimensional entity with aims of total world destruction...</div> </div> </div> </div>You due know that the faustians are the exact opposite of &quot;Save the world through hugs and kisses&quot;, they are quite litterally faustian demons who tempt mortals to steal their souls. Also their biggest enemy is the earthbound who are extra dimensional entities vying for the worlds destruction by taking over seemingly unaffiliated groups of multi-national corporations.... Oh Wait!<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, it would be very hard to distinguish between pentex and an earthbound cult(the two groups probably even work together in some instances). I wouldn't fault a fallen for getting the two confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T19:25:34-08:00","id":778758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=778739#post778739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You due know that the faustians are the exact opposite of &quot;Save the world through hugs and kisses&quot;, they are quite litterally faustian demons who tempt mortals to steal their souls. Also their biggest enemy is the earthbound who are extra dimensional entities vying for the worlds destruction by taking over seemingly unaffiliated groups of multi-national corporations.... Oh Wait!<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, it would be very hard to distinguish between pentex and an earthbound cult(the two groups probably even work together in some instances). I wouldn't fault a fallen for getting the two confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it wouldn't be difficult at all. I'd imagine that the cults do way less paperwork, for one. They also let you wear scary robes on Friday. With Pentex subsidiaries, it's all business, all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T20:01:10-08:00","id":778776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=778758#post778758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it wouldn't be difficult at all. I'd imagine that the cults do way less paperwork, for one. They also let you wear scary robes on Friday. With Pentex subsidiaries, it's all business, all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure pentex has casual Friday's provided your department hit quota","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T21:13:08-08:00","id":778794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=778776#post778776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure pentex has casual Friday's provided your department hit quota</div> </div> </div> </div>The Earthbound corps don't have Casual Friday, they have Cultish Friday. Pentex looks down on the practicing of dressing in robes and engaging in ceremonies as being backward and unprofessional. Oddly, a quote from the Francesco in the 2nd edition Book of the Wyrm sums it up nicely. &quot;Yeah, yeah, it took you three hours and five sacrifices to summon the Urge Wyrm of Greed. Big deal. I can speed-dial him on my cell phone.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T02:40:26-08:00","id":778875,"title":"","content":"just remember, your soul and your sanity; much like casual/cultist/pizza/infant Friday are a privilege. Not a right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T04:18:44-08:00","id":778908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=778758#post778758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it wouldn't be difficult at all. I'd imagine that the cults do way less paperwork, for one. They also let you wear scary robes on Friday. With Pentex subsidiaries, it's all business, all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh, I'm pretty sure the thralls that they can't harvest faith from are the ones running the day job. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T02:46:11-08:00","id":780461,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that Pentex almost surely has the support of Wyrmish Awakened Mages (the Malfean Nephandi faction; they walk the Black Spiral and team up with Black Spiral Dancers). If they become aware that someone is trying to take over or destroy one of their most powerful fronts/tools - and being Mages, in all likelihood they <i>will</i> become aware - the Fallen will have True Magick to contend with. Was it written anywhere whether Mages with Spirit can affect Fallen, and to what extent? Though attacking Fallen directly might not even be needed - setting other Fallen or even Earthbound against them might work, as well.<br /> The Syndicate also had fingers in Pentex, but I think this changed in M20 Syndicate book. The senior Pentex executives do resemble a Nephandic Syndicate to me; with stuff like having the Urge Wyrm of Greed on a speed dial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-05-2015, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T06:54:38-08:00","id":780539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=780461#post780461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that Pentex almost surely has the support of Wyrmish Awakened Mages (the Malfean Nephandi faction; they walk the Black Spiral and team up with Black Spiral Dancers). If they become aware that someone is trying to take over or destroy one of their most powerful fronts/tools - and being Mages, in all likelihood they <i>will</i> become aware - the Fallen will have True Magick to contend with. Was it written anywhere whether Mages with Spirit can affect Fallen, and to what extent? Though attacking Fallen directly might not even be needed - setting other Fallen or even Earthbound against them might work, as well.<br /> The Syndicate also had fingers in Pentex, but I think this changed in M20 Syndicate book. The senior Pentex executives do resemble a Nephandic Syndicate to me; with stuff like having the Urge Wyrm of Greed on a speed dial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Francesco is a Consultant BSD, actually, and the BotW gets by the entire time without really making any references to Mage at all. When they're pulling strings and getting their agendas done, it isn't a form of magic, it's just infrastructure doing what it does. Mage calls that magick, but it's pretty much alone among the games for doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T07:53:48-08:00","id":780553,"title":"","content":"Yes, but I assumed that since it's a crossover already, the other lines can also get properly involved. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So Pentex's executives, instead of being 'humans with Wyrm's blessings', could be Awakened Mages with a Nephandi/Syndicate mix of a Paradigm. Peter Culliford is several hundred years old, so I think it can fit.<br /> <br /> The reason - at least if you buy the Technocracy's party line - why Syndicate's management is Magick is because they are just <i>that</i> good at picking the right moment and the right things to do...which I do admit is kind of weird/unbelievable. In this case I'd have the hypothetical Pentex executive Mages use theories - that are 3/4 scientific &amp; 1/4 philosophical/mystical - about how causing misery and suffering <i><b>is</b></i> the way to maximize profits - if one is willing to go all the way through with it. Complete with macabre Power Point presentations about how to best do it (You know all those options that PP has, like text and pictures popping in and out in various ways..about time someone used them! All I'm seeing those days is vanilla slides without any animations.) And grotesque Excel spreadsheets in which Banes play with the data - like changing the equation for a column just a little bit.. - to suggest &amp; guide courses of actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-05-2015, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T09:23:42-08:00","id":780586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=780553#post780553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but I assumed that since it's a crossover already, the other lines can also get properly involved. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So Pentex's executives, instead of being 'humans with Wyrm's blessings', could be Awakened Mages with a Nephandi/Syndicate mix of a Paradigm. Peter Culliford is several hundred years old, so I think it can fit.<br /> <br /> The reason - at least if you buy the Technocracy's party line - why Syndicate's management is Magick is because they are just <i>that</i> good at picking the right moment and the right things to do...which I do admit is kind of weird/unbelievable. In this case I'd have the hypothetical Pentex executive Mages use theories - that are 3/4 scientific &amp; 1/4 philosophical/mystical - about how causing misery and suffering <i><b>is</b></i> the way to maximize profits - if one is willing to go all the way through with it. Complete with macabre Power Point presentations about how to best do it (You know all those options that PP has, like text and pictures popping in and out in various ways..about time someone used them! All I'm seeing those days is vanilla slides without any animations.) And grotesque Excel spreadsheets in which Banes play with the data - like changing the equation for a column just a little bit.. - to suggest &amp; guide courses of actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The would massively de-complicate a fixture of things that you have to deal with in Werewolf: being benevolent and eschewing activity that would produce more shit in the world is a hard road by its own nature, not the result of magickal tinkering with the cosmos. Given that magick is rarer than people who do shitty things, it would be a stunning reversal of theme about how you can't just stop Pentex by killing a few key executives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T12:09:57-08:00","id":780652,"title":"","content":"If some Fallen wanted to destroy Pentex, they are possible the only ones who can do so by going into direct competition with them.<br /> <br /> You'll want a few Devils and Defilers as your executives and representatives, a few Fiends to advise, and a whole lot of Malefactors. Assuming demons have been roming around since about 2000 that gives them about 15 years to adapt to the modern world. Malefactors can possibly invent technology either better than or cheaper than Pentex products, and erode their market share. Why get the Banebox720 when the Faithstation is just all-around better? And hey, I hear that Diamond Road picked up all those abandoned Black Dog games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:32:37-08:00","id":780764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=780652#post780652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If some Fallen wanted to destroy Pentex, they are possible the only ones who can do so by going into direct competition with them.<br /> <br /> You'll want a few Devils and Defilers as your executives and representatives, a few Fiends to advise, and a whole lot of Malefactors. Assuming demons have been roming around since about 2000 that gives them about 15 years to adapt to the modern world. Malefactors can possibly invent technology either better than or cheaper than Pentex products, and erode their market share. Why get the Banebox720 when the Faithstation is just all-around better? And hey, I hear that Diamond Road picked up all those abandoned Black Dog games.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Going into direct competition with all Pentex subsidiaries&quot; = &quot;Can start a major ripple in the entire world's economy on a lark&quot;. I very much doubt that there enough Fallen to accomplish this, given the other business in which they typically find themselves embroiled. Their internal struggles tend to put them in a bad place when it comes to trying; playing the corporate game, in particular, is likely to load any given demon up on Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T21:21:53-08:00","id":780896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=780652#post780652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If some Fallen wanted to destroy Pentex, they are possible the only ones who can do so by going into direct competition with them.<br /> <br /> You'll want a few Devils and Defilers as your executives and representatives, a few Fiends to advise, and a whole lot of Malefactors. Assuming demons have been roming around since about 2000 that gives them about 15 years to adapt to the modern world. Malefactors can possibly invent technology either better than or cheaper than Pentex products, and erode their market share. Why get the Banebox720 when the Faithstation is just all-around better? And hey, I hear that Diamond Road picked up all those abandoned Black Dog games.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is basically what I was thinking. Given their ability to wield truly earth shattering powers with rituals provided they can get enough humans to participate and the nature of their powers. Also, it seems like this is exactly the sort of thing, given their long term goals of openly ruling the world, that they will want to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=780764#post780764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Going into direct competition with all Pentex subsidiaries&quot; = &quot;Can start a major ripple in the entire world's economy on a lark&quot;. I very much doubt that there enough Fallen to accomplish this, given the other business in which they typically find themselves embroiled. Their internal struggles tend to put them in a bad place when it comes to trying; playing the corporate game, in particular, is likely to load any given demon up on Torment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a lark. The Fallen were brought in to the WoD specifically to be a game changer, and MOST want to go back to ruling the world. And the feasibility depends on the state of the Fallen in your WoD. The Factions in the Storytellers Guide weren't at war with each other yet, except the Raveners, and even then the game doesn't seem to imply full scale war as a united faction yet. If the Faustians decided the path to global conquest was money, a reasonable assumption, I can see them giving Pentex a real run for its money. Especially, when you throw high level rituals into the mix, the Fallen are only limited by the amount of human Faith they have available. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T21:29:16-08:00","id":780899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=780896#post780896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a lark. The Fallen were brought in to the WoD specifically to be a game changer, and MOST want to go back to ruling the world. And the feasibility depends on the state of the Fallen in your WoD. The Factions in the Storytellers Guide weren't at war with each other yet, except the Raveners, and even then the game doesn't seem to imply full scale war as a united faction yet. If the Faustians decided the path to global conquest was money, a reasonable assumption, I can see them giving Pentex a real run for its money. Especially, when you throw high level rituals into the mix, the Fallen are only limited by the amount of human Faith they have available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Faith, or money - what do you think is scarce in most WoD games? As for being a game-changer, they never even showed up to the game, as far as most other games were concerned. They might as well have never existed at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:54:27-08:00","id":780948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=780899#post780899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Faith, or money - what do you think is scarce in most WoD games? As for being a game-changer, they never even showed up to the game, as far as most other games were concerned. They might as well have never existed at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because they showed up at the last second before everything went dark. But the Fallen or the Earthbound could easily have been the one's who ended the WoD if that is how you wanted to play the ToJ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T23:17:02-08:00","id":780956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=780948#post780948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Because they showed up at the last second before everything went dark. But the Fallen or the Earthbound could easily have been the one's who ended the WoD if that is how you wanted to play the ToJ.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no &quot;the&quot; WoD, and if they had set up Demon as being the end for everything, that would have been immensely souring, to say the least. It's quite fortunate that it was easily written out instead, because the shared world stopped being a neat thing several adventures into Haight's story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T23:44:54-08:00","id":780967,"title":"","content":"Hunter had a few interesting moments, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T06:14:12-08:00","id":781097,"title":"","content":"I do think that a conflict between a Fallen's corporation and Pentex, given any level of crossover in a chronicle, is very likely to happen at any time.<br /> <br /> But from that, everything else will be dependent on circumstances and your particular crossover.<br /> <br /> Lets see some possibilities, though. First, the Earthbound are really the first more probable to deal with Pentex. Sure, some Devils from any faction could begin the Fallen Co., but it is more likely to have a greater number of those being ruled by Earthbound (including through enslaved Devils). Them it depends largely on said Earthbound. Certainly Pentex and other Wyrm allies of it could be interested in using those ancient gods, but the Earthbound are a diverse and crazy bunch. Some can ally with the Wyrm, but a lot will either see it as a rival and enemy for the control of the world, and some will simply be too paranoid to deal with it in any fashion but obliteration (not that they <u>will</u> accomplish such). Not to mention the ones that simply see things through serious delusions and simply think they are in some sort of epic myth. Some of the Mad Gods are quite Mad.<br /> <br /> From this point, the &quot;human&quot; Fallen can get involved in diverse ways. The Raveners can see Pentex as quite an ally, or simply not giving it much attention (except a large berth if they think it is a front for an Earthbound. The distinction between a demonic cult and Pentex can only be so clear <u>when</u> you find out the daily activities of the inner circle of the corp, and it is unlikely to happen so soon). In the worst scenario for them, Pentex is at least making it all the easier to destroy the world, if not destroying it outright, and even Raveners think on the long run.<br /> <br /> Most of the other Factions are likely to be against Pentex sooner or later. Even for the more Tormented Faustians, they are still competing for resources. Pentex causes suffering in all too subtle ways, being disinterested on the overt misery that births Faith. They want people to only have faith in their products and in continual consumption, the Faustians can use it, but eventually they will try to at least take the Pentex more overtly to themselves. And probably they won't be very happy if they actually find about the Wyrm. Luciferans want to fight &quot;for humanity&quot;, and probably also won't be very fond of a company making their source of Faith so miserable. Reconcilers are quite obvious. Even some Criptics will fight it, be it for personal interest or personal morality, be it to learn about Pentex by &quot;dissecting&quot; it. And even the Raveners can try to infiltrate and take over the corporation.<br /> <br /> The presence of other splats in Pentex is a question of personal taste. It is unlikely that most of it isn't human, but it does have room for other splats, actually to all of them. I would only make it another iteration of the &quot;Hydra&quot; thing: the supernatural creatures of every kind are powerful heads, but Pentex is the immortal body of the beast. As long as somewhere a lone head remembers the ways of the Wyrm, the company can just survive the entire purge of the high echelons and will continue polluting the world and making it miserable. It isn't about powerful heads. It is about filthy lucre, and the efficiency in making profit by shitting in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:35:50-08:00","id":781253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=780764#post780764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Going into direct competition with all Pentex subsidiaries&quot; = &quot;Can start a major ripple in the entire world's economy on a lark&quot;. I very much doubt that there enough Fallen to accomplish this, given the other business in which they typically find themselves embroiled. Their internal struggles tend to put them in a bad place when it comes to trying; playing the corporate game, in particular, is likely to load any given demon up on Torment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said can, not will. The Fallen can go into direct competition with all Pentex subsidiaries, assuming you can get a significant number of the non-crazy ones to work together. In reality any particular Pentex subsidiary isn't competing with Fallen Inc but with a company only acting in their area of expertise, which a determined group of Fallen could set up (think of it as a possible campaign goal for a group). In all likelihood the Fallen do not care about Pentex though. Pentex is pretty clearly a symptom, not a cause, and the Fallen could do a lot more by targeting whatever it is that is causing Pentex. So Fallen who wish to improve the world could just ignore Pentex, while I see some who don't care as possibly being fairly interested in this 'controlled crash' scenario Pentex has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:42:29-08:00","id":781267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781253#post781253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I said can, not will. The Fallen can go into direct competition with all Pentex subsidiaries, assuming you can get a significant number of the non-crazy ones to work together. In reality any particular Pentex subsidiary isn't competing with Fallen Inc but with a company only acting in their area of expertise, which a determined group of Fallen could set up (think of it as a possible campaign goal for a group). In all likelihood the Fallen do not care about Pentex though. Pentex is pretty clearly a symptom, not a cause, and the Fallen could do a lot more by targeting whatever it is that is causing Pentex. So Fallen who wish to improve the world could just ignore Pentex, while I see some who don't care as possibly being fairly interested in this 'controlled crash' scenario Pentex has.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one can ignore the subsidiaries under Pentex. They make up a huge slice of the worldwide economy in Werewolf's corner of the WoD. Out-competing them isn't happening, because they can always act to squash Fallen competition, say by buying out the rights to whatever the Fallen are making and sitting on them, pulling strings to get the government to crack down on their operations (they bought most governments, so they won't face the same scrutiny very easily), or just sending fomori death squads at the Fallen with no end. More likely, they would find out that their competitors are some kind of spiritual entity that often has an aura which, like most fomori, the Garou find distasteful, and then act like they're buddy-buddy with Fallen Corp. Then the upper management lights cigars with twenties while the Garou get lured into shredding the hosts of the Fallen to bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T13:22:05-08:00","id":781294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781267#post781267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one can ignore the subsidiaries under Pentex.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends, it is a legitimate response to decide that getting rid of Pentex will only cause Pentex 2: Electric Banealo to appear. It's possible a Fallen might decide it's better to act against the Wyrm directly than Pentex, or fix societal problems, or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They make up a huge slice of the worldwide economy in Werewolf's corner of the WoD. Out-competing them isn't happening, because they can always act to squash Fallen competition, say by buying out the rights to whatever the Fallen are making and sitting on them, pulling strings to get the government to crack down on their operations (they bought most governments, so they won't face the same scrutiny very easily), or just sending fomori death squads at the Fallen with no end. More likely, they would find out that their competitors are some kind of spiritual entity that often has an aura which, like most fomori, the Garou find distasteful, and then act like they're buddy-buddy with Fallen Corp. Then the upper management lights cigars with twenties while the Garou get lured into shredding the hosts of the Fallen to bits. </div> </div> </div>I'm going to leave up the buying out the rights/siccing the government on them, because as a Demon fan I prefer Pentex to be powerful but not almighty. Fomori death squads require subjects to create, and as Demons have a high proportion of social splats (I think at least 4 out of 7 houses are focused on socialising? Defliers, Devils, and Fiends definitely are) or like to work at a distance (Malefactors being a key example) it might be hard to track down the actual demons doing it.<br /> <br /> I also think Demons having a fomori-like aura is a large assumption to make. I'd actually peg the Elohim, even the Fallen, as more like Weaver spirits than Wyrm, although with a slight possibility of Wyld. (I actually like the idea that the Creator and the Triat are two different versions of the same being, the Creator seems to be gone because he's insane and partially traped.) Still not what the Garou might want, but less likely to be death packs sent at them and more a 'can you please stop' first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T14:12:41-08:00","id":781313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781294#post781294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends, it is a legitimate response to decide that getting rid of Pentex will only cause Pentex 2: Electric Banealo to appear. It's possible a Fallen might decide it's better to act against the Wyrm directly than Pentex, or fix societal problems, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>At which point they would probably be unmade, because even the Earthbound still have stats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going to leave up the buying out the rights/siccing the government on them, because as a Demon fan I prefer Pentex to be powerful but not almighty. Fomori death squads require subjects to create, and as Demons have a high proportion of social splats (I think at least 4 out of 7 houses are focused on socialising? Defliers, Devils, and Fiends definitely are) or like to work at a distance (Malefactors being a key example) it might be hard to track down the actual demons doing it.<br /> <br /> I also think Demons having a fomori-like aura is a large assumption to make. I'd actually peg the Elohim, even the Fallen, as more like Weaver spirits than Wyrm, although with a slight possibility of Wyld. (I actually like the idea that the Creator and the Triat are two different versions of the same being, the Creator seems to be gone because he's insane and partially traped.) Still not what the Garou might want, but less likely to be death packs sent at them and more a 'can you please stop' first. </div> </div> </div>It's not almighty, but it is very well entrenched, and fighting it with its own systems is not a plan that can succeed very easily. You basically depend on Pentex subsidiaries to fight Pentex subsidiaries, which introduces no end of headaches, roadblocks, setbacks, and untenable positions.<br /> <br /> As for Fallen and taint, enough high-Torment examples probably exist to sour the Garou on them all, much like their beef with vampires. They rate as a more immediate threat because they can probably do more things expected of spirits than vampires and, being possessed, would highly resemble a type of fomor to the embattled, paranoid sensibilities of the werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-06-2015, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T19:49:33-08:00","id":781496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781313#post781313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At which point they would probably be unmade, because even the Earthbound still have stats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always found the &quot;So powerful it doesn't have stats&quot; cop out to be just that, a cop out. It was made by the WOD writers not because they couldn't attach stats to said being, but because they didn't want players beating npc's important to the meta and actually changing anything in their world of darkness games(like in revised when they created maelstrom and over-wrote all their material that allowed a player to be something other than &quot;just&quot; another vamp/mage/werwolf completely powerless in the hierarchy of the world.)<br /> <br /> Not that I want the players to be the center of the universe or some &quot;chosen one&quot;(I already get enough of that from recent video games), but there should at least be the possiblity if they put up enough of a fight(like give the wyrm 30 dice in all stats and make it difficulty 10 to hit with 1, 2, and 3's counting as botches). I personally design my games around the &quot;nothing's impossible, some things are just difficulty 25&quot; style of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T20:34:35-08:00","id":781511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781496#post781496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I always found the &quot;So powerful it doesn't have stats&quot; cop out to be just that, a cop out. It was made by the WOD writers not because they couldn't attach stats to said being, but because they didn't want players beating npc's important to the meta and actually changing anything in their world of darkness games(like in revised when they created maelstrom and over-wrote all their material that allowed a player to be something other than &quot;just&quot; another vamp/mage/werwolf completely powerless in the hierarchy of the world.)<br /> <br /> Not that I want the players to be the center of the universe or some &quot;chosen one&quot;(I already get enough of that from recent video games), but there should at least be the possiblity if they put up enough of a fight(like give the wyrm 30 dice in all stats and make it difficulty 10 to hit with 1, 2, and 3's counting as botches). I personally design my games around the &quot;nothing's impossible, some things are just difficulty 25&quot; style of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-statted beings can be used well to focus characters on a particular scale. That this method might have fallen far short of this goal does not remove their potential for use. Earthbound are things that can be tangled with sans the need for plot devices; Maeljin, however, have much more involved requirements for engagement, defeat, and destruction.<br /> <br /> Also, the Wyrm kind of doesn't have stats because it's more like the Dark Side of the Force than an actual character. That's the other possibility for not statting something; it'd be like giving mechanics for punching gravity. Cue irritating Mage rant about why you should totally be able to punch gravity in 3, 2, 1...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T21:39:39-08:00","id":781549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781267#post781267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one can ignore the subsidiaries under Pentex. They make up a huge slice of the worldwide economy in Werewolf's corner of the WoD. Out-competing them isn't happening, because they can always act to squash Fallen competition, say by buying out the rights to whatever the Fallen are making and sitting on them, pulling strings to get the government to crack down on their operations (they bought most governments, so they won't face the same scrutiny very easily), or just sending fomori death squads at the Fallen with no end. More likely, they would find out that their competitors are some kind of spiritual entity that often has an aura which, like most fomori, the Garou find distasteful, and then act like they're buddy-buddy with Fallen Corp. Then the upper management lights cigars with twenties while the Garou get lured into shredding the hosts of the Fallen to bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex is powerful, but there are still competing companies right? I haven't really looked that deeply into the BotW. Are they really THE world economy? Microsoft, IBM, Apple, Facebook and every other company in the world at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 12-07-2015, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T21:57:08-08:00","id":781556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781549#post781549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pentex is powerful, but there are still competing companies right? I haven't really looked that deeply into the BotW. Are they really THE world economy? Microsoft, IBM, Apple, Facebook and every other company in the world at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really the &quot;entire&quot; economy, just some of the top companies in their perspective fields, they have a slight edge on the competition due to their &quot;backer&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T07:04:57-08:00","id":781687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781556#post781556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Not really the &quot;entire&quot; economy, just some of the top companies in their perspective fields, they have a slight edge on the competition due to their &quot;backer&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's if you don't count crossovers, Pentex is only the head of everything in WTA. If you were to splice in other series like say mage or vampire, then they'd be on equal ground competing with technocracy owned businesses or backed by the camarilla. The moment you start crossovers then the big bad from one game is no longer the end all be all anymore, they're just Another big bad.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781511#post781511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Non-statted beings can be used well to focus characters on a particular scale. That this method might have fallen far short of this goal does not remove their potential for use. Earthbound are things that can be tangled with sans the need for plot devices; Maeljin, however, have much more involved requirements for engagement, defeat, and destruction.<br /> <br /> Also, the Wyrm kind of doesn't have stats because it's more like the Dark Side of the Force than an actual character. That's the other possibility for not statting something; it'd be like giving mechanics for punching gravity. Cue irritating Mage rant about why you should totally be able to punch gravity in 3, 2, 1...</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Wyrm isn't entropy, it's the spiritual representation entropy(think of it like this, you can't punch the nation of the united states, but you can punch the president), It's just a powerful spirit in the umbra the represents the Concept of entropy. It may be a powerful celestine that's stuck in a plane of pure entropy, but it is not entropy itself, just a representative(which kind of puts a hole in the whole &quot;kill the wyrm&quot; to save the world thing as a new wyrm will just form from the fact that the concept of entropy still exists.(but hopefully this one will be less evil))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T07:23:07-08:00","id":781691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781687#post781687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's if you don't count crossovers, Pentex is only the head of everything in WTA. If you were to splice in other series like say mage or vampire, then they'd be on equal ground competing with technocracy owned businesses or backed by the camarilla. The moment you start crossovers then the big bad from one game is no longer the end all be all anymore, they're just Another big bad.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually. Pentex isn't the head of everything in Werewolf; it's just one huge antagonist organization. There are quite a few others. It is really big and very threatening, though, and has entrenched itself in the public in a way that Black Spiral Dancers and most cults haven't, kind of like the Guild from Exalted, but in a high modern industrial form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except the Wyrm isn't entropy, it's the spiritual representation entropy(think of it like this, you can't punch the nation of the united states, but you can punch the president), It's just a powerful spirit in the umbra the represents the Concept of entropy. It may be a powerful celestine that's stuck in a plane of pure entropy, but it is not entropy itself, just a representative(which kind of puts a hole in the whole &quot;kill the wyrm&quot; to save the world thing as a new wyrm will just form from the fact that the concept of entropy still exists.(but hopefully this one will be less evil)) </div> </div> </div>The comparison was made by the former developer, way, way back when. While not those &quot;essential concepts&quot; as we understand them (and I would say entropy, because that's overused in the cWoD and, like a certain song about irony, never really matched the actual meaning of the word), they are spirits that make these concepts possible in Werewolf's animistic setting assumptions. Also, under no circumstances is the Wyrm as small as a Celestine; when the Fera don't agree about the place of Gaia and the Triat, they all agree that the Triat ranges from being another order of being just beyond Celestines, to beings that created the cosmos, always higher in rank than Luna, Helios, etc.<br /> <br /> So, no, it isn't really just another powerful spirit. It's such a vast one that even the spirits that have to use avatars to communicate consider it too vast with which to relate. And you don't just pop one and then wait for another to form; that's only how Incarnae work, as a quite explicit notion in the text; Celestines and higher enable something, and once they go, so does that something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:07:09-08:00","id":781780,"title":"","content":"In Werewolf Pentex might be the big bad corporation, in Vampire it might just be a regular megacorp like a giant Google, in Demon Pentex might not be a problem on the Fallen's scale (either too big if you take WTA into account, or too small otherwise. In the view of the WoD as a whole, you've convinced me that Fallen Corp couldn't take them down, but I think if you let the Fallen use smaller corporations in a decentralised system because they aren't actually working with each other they can give Pentex a run for their money.<br /> <br /> On the subject of 'too awesome for stats', I only think there are four beings in the WoD who get that: the full Weaver, the full Wyld, the full Wyrm, and the Creator (who in my WoD is the Fallen's name for the Triat in harmony, they aren't so creeped out by the Umbra existing as the Umbra not being a part of the mortal world). Everybody else, such as the Defiler Wyrm, Eater of Souls, the Neverborn, and Caine can be given stats, but only Caine has any limits (his highest stat in my world is a 10 compared to the others being 15+, but his lots of 10s and varied disciplines make him deadly, as he has several unique ones).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T13:53:09-08:00","id":781827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781780#post781780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of 'too awesome for stats', I only think there are four beings in the WoD who get that: the full Weaver, the full Wyld, the full Wyrm, and the Creator (who in my WoD is the Fallen's name for the Triat in harmony, they aren't so creeped out by the Umbra existing as the Umbra not being a part of the mortal world). Everybody else, such as the Defiler Wyrm, Eater of Souls, the Neverborn, and Caine can be given stats, but only Caine has any limits (his highest stat in my world is a 10 compared to the others being 15+, but his lots of 10s and varied disciplines make him deadly, as he has several unique ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything <i>can </i>be given stats, but there is a reason the books don't. The Antediluvians are not just big monsters you can beat with a stick, and Caine and the Neverborn or the heads of the Wyrm are beyond <i>them</i>. Saying 'I think everything should be stated out' just sounds silly. Why bother? Whether you are rolling a thousand dice verses five hundred, the outcome is the same. The 'gods' win, unless you have a big shiny plotpoint in your favor. They aren't beings meant to be fought directly... punching out Cthluhu doesn't make you awesome, it just cheapens the whole setting.<br /> <br /> The powerful inhabitants of Malfeas in the Book of the Wyrm are good examples of how to handle 'stat-less' gribblies: outline what they want, who their minions are, what their unique powers do, and maybe some rumored ways to kill them. That is enough. We don't kneed to know what the Nameless Angel of Despair's soak pool is, and even if we did, that would be sort of missing the point of including the Nameless Angel in the first place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-07-2015, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T14:31:51-08:00","id":781840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781827#post781827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything <i>can </i>be given stats, but there is a reason the books don't. The Antediluvians are not just big monsters you can beat with a stick, and Caine and the Neverborn or the heads of the Wyrm are beyond <i>them</i>. Saying 'I think everything should be stated out' just sounds silly. Why bother? Whether you are rolling a thousand dice verses five hundred, the outcome is the same. The 'gods' win, unless you have a big shiny plotpoint in your favor. They aren't beings meant to be fought directly... punching out Cthluhu doesn't make you awesome, it just cheapens the whole setting.<br /> <br /> The powerful inhabitants of Malfeas in the Book of the Wyrm are good examples of how to handle 'stat-less' gribblies: outline what they want, who their minions are, what their unique powers do, and maybe some rumored ways to kill them. That is enough. We don't kneed to know what the Nameless Angel of Despair's soak pool is, and even if we did, that would be sort of missing the point of including the Nameless Angel in the first place...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy, I think this comes from us having different viewpoints. If the PCs are going to meet a 'statless' creature, I'm going to give them stats so that the PCs at least have a fighting chance. Sure, powerful monster XII might have 20 soak dice whereas the PCs only are rolling about 8 dice on damage, but that rare thing hurting it is my way of saying to my players 'you can beat this if you act smart', because if the PCs come up with a clever plan to unbalance the universe even more by killing one of the aspects of the Wyrm, I believe that they deserve to have a shot. Maybe 1/100 or less, depends on how smart the plan is, but a shot. If you think you can beat any of the Antediluvians with a big stick, just remember that they might have the level 10 discipline 'remove stick from existence, along with user and all of the user's friends and family who are not currently of use to me'. But you might be able to, say, force them back into Torpor by dropping them down a very deep pit and into the mantle (...which is a totally legitimate mage tactic now that I think about it, it just requires a lot of prep).<br /> <br /> Some people like some creatures to be undefeatable without plot. This is fine, but comes from a STing style very different to my own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T14:57:58-08:00","id":781858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781840#post781840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people like some creatures to be undefeatable without plot. This is fine, but comes from a STing style very different to my own.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a style that leads to twinks and lucky rolls eliminating something that has been plaguing the setting for thousands of years and for what solutions are not in punching it harder but actually being clever and doing something inspired about it. If something is untouchable and the characters encounter it, it is untouchable and they should be running the fuck away until they figure out something better then just tussling with it. It's a style that suits D&amp;D much more than any game of the WOD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:07:15-08:00","id":781864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781840#post781840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some people like some creatures to be undefeatable without plot. This is fine, but comes from a STing style very different to my own.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are defeating Eater of Souls or a Neverborn without plot, <i>ipso facto</i> you will not have much of a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:10:32-08:00","id":781867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781858#post781858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a style that leads to twinks and lucky rolls eliminating something that has been plaguing the setting for thousands of years and for what solutions are not in punching it harder but actually being clever and doing something inspired about it. If something is untouchable and the characters encounter it, it is untouchable and they should be running the fuck away until they figure out something better then just tussling with it. It's a style that suits D&amp;D much more than any game of the WOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, look, it's the 'your style doesn't fit with the WoD' argument. I've been getting it ever since I tried to run a non dungeon crawling game in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Again, I prefer to have my 'it's powerful and so you'd better run away from it' expressed through stats and powers. Maybe it's immune to any damage not done by mistletoe cut by a blind man and bathed in three day old goat's milk, but instead of being 'you can't hurt it without that, nananenana' it's 'it has a power saying all soak tests automatically succeed unless [attack method blah]' is used.<br /> <br /> And very occasionally, due to the nature of dice pools and the fact that non-PCs aren't strictly wedded to 7 health levels, I can have a creature that can survive the luckiest hit in the universe just through being goddam tough, and not because ST fiat says so. Because I like to roll with what the dice give me. Obviously you don't that's fine, and I respect that, but stop yeling 'no, wrongbadfun!' at somebody preferring to run big bad monsters in a way you don't. Much awesome can be had when the players have to deal with the (positive and negative consequences) of taking down a behemoth through pure luck. This isn't a computer game where the monster has to survive so that the PCs can only kill it when they've done another 2 chapters of the main quest, if the PCs manage to kill a beast with 15 soak dice and 60 health levels that deals twenty dice of damage per attack through quick thinking and exploiting the environment, then I won't complain. If they do enough research and come with a way to nullify the uber-monster's immunities, I want to be able to give them a fight, not a 'well it's still uberpowerful so it kills you'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:25:45-08:00","id":781879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781867#post781867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, look, it's the 'your style doesn't fit with the WoD' argument. I've been getting it ever since I tried to run a non dungeon crawling game in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Again, I prefer to have my 'it's powerful and so you'd better run away from it' expressed through stats and powers. Maybe it's immune to any damage not done by mistletoe cut by a blind man and bathed in three day old goat's milk, but instead of being 'you can't hurt it without that, nananenana' it's 'it has a power saying all soak tests automatically succeed unless [attack method blah]' is used.<br /> <br /> And very occasionally, due to the nature of dice pools and the fact that non-PCs aren't strictly wedded to 7 health levels, I can have a creature that can survive the luckiest hit in the universe just through being goddam tough, and not because ST fiat says so. Because I like to roll with what the dice give me. Obviously you don't that's fine, and I respect that, but stop yeling 'no, wrongbadfun!' at somebody preferring to run big bad monsters in a way you don't. Much awesome can be had when the players have to deal with the (positive and negative consequences) of taking down a behemoth through pure luck. This isn't a computer game where the monster has to survive so that the PCs can only kill it when they've done another 2 chapters of the main quest, if the PCs manage to kill a beast with 15 soak dice and 60 health levels that deals twenty dice of damage per attack through quick thinking and exploiting the environment, then I won't complain. If they do enough research and come with a way to nullify the uber-monster's immunities, I want to be able to give them a fight, not a 'well it's still uberpowerful so it kills you'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your method either forces people to go through the motions to do jack shit to something - which is not fun. Or it leads to total plot derailment due to freak dice or unhealthy twinkery. Which of those two things seems conductive to a good story?<br /> <br /> Punching problems does not fix them. It tends to make them worse. Especially in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:55:40-08:00","id":781902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781879#post781879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your method either forces people to go through the motions to do jack shit to something - which is not fun. Or it leads to total plot derailment due to freak dice or unhealthy twinkery. Which of those two things seems conductive to a good story?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Spoken like somebody who has never turned up to run a game with a starting scenario and a folder of NPCs.<br /> <br /> I need to reorder my NPCs folder...<br /> <br /> My point that I have a completely different STing style to you. Maybe you like to plot out everything in advance, I like to throw caution to the winds and improvise a story, because it's fun. I did try to imply that I either let players have a chance to work it out before hand or to be able to win by exploiting everything at their disposal, but then again I hate invincible monsters, even in my novels (the closest I've gotten is a monster likely to ignore damage due to their biology. So a monster might be really powerful, but if the PCs are facing it they have at least a slim chance of winning.]<br /> <br /> If they win they haven't 'derailed the plot', they've 'taken the story in a new direction'. Frankly the use of the word 'derail' implies a lot to me, but that might be because my games are very loosely plotted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Punching problems does not fix them. It tends to make them worse. Especially in the WoD. </div> </div> </div>Problems can be a lot more complex than an invincible monster. 'You can't even fight the monster' is really annoying, because very occasionally I want a game where the PCs are awesome badasses who solve the problem by punching it in the modern world, but don't want to run Scion or Mutants and Masterminds, at which point World of Darkness works. Or I want a game where the PCs have to try hard to defeat even basic enemies, and I can make WoD work for that campaign as well. Whether or not killing the giant monster makes the situation better or worse depends on which style I'm going for, but the giant monster is rarely the most troublesome aspect of the problem. That's generally finding the guys doing stuff hidden in human society doing the really damaging stuff, or occasionally getting the PCs to work together.<br /> <br /> Also, I like a good boss fight. If, at some point, I want to run a heroic Werewolf the Apocalypse chronicle featuring the Apocalypse, having the final battle being against an aspect of the Wyrm could be great. Have the Rank 5 PCs and a bunch of Rank 5 allies in a giant battle with it!<br /> <br /> But again, as I've been saying, I have a completely different STing style. It might not be 'the plot says X so X must happen', but there are other ways to run a story-based game. I happen to like games like Fate which give the players power as much as I like the crunchiness and simulationist nature of the cWoD, and it's easy to let my players have power: improvise. You don't have to, you can plot or improvise, railroad or sandbox*, whatever you want, and it's as valid as any other style no matter what game you're in. This isn't 'dungeon crawling versus courtly intrigue', this is 'is the story generated by the ST or the game?' I like to have it generated by the game, but I will add in that I played in a highly enjoyable tightly plotted rather railroad heavy campaign, as well as a horrible one that was presented as a sandbox but cause problems whenever we did what the GM didn't want.<br /> <br /> You are just screaming 'no, that is unfun, do not do that' whereas I can say from experience that players can have fun with exactly that. I was once in a group where we almost 'punched out' a literally fallen angel by force of will, and would still have won without the GM's plot token (once I made the discovery that the angel's shield only affected physical objects, not exorcisms).<br /> <br /> *not the same difference as plotting or improvising, but I'm too tired to explain.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:55:00-08:00","id":781946,"title":"","content":"I think that such method may lead to problems with powergaming. For a thing, it <i>seems</i> to reward powergaming. 15 points in everything isn't really very impressive from a powergamer point of view, giving the <i>impression </i>that you can defeat anything with a strong fighter. (Really, 15 in everything it's still pretty weak. The avatar of Fenris, a mere fragment of a mere Incarna, has 20 in Rage. 100-1000 seems more appropriate for the really big things, the destroyer of worlds shouldn't die by falling a very tall cliff).<br /> <br /> I think that style leads the storyteller to situations in which, because of the skill of the players building killer machines, he will have to start creating Disciplines (or other powers) like this one...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think you can beat any of the Antediluvians with a big stick, just remember that they might have the level 10 discipline 'remove stick from existence, along with user and all of the user's friends and family who are not currently of use to me'.</div> </div> </div> </div>...in order to prevent characters from slaying everything, starting an &quot;arms race&quot; with his players that he will likely win...most of the time...(after all, giving an Antediluvian a &quot;surprise&quot; Discipline that he hadn't five minutes earlier equals denying his defeat by narrative means...which his players might find injust, where they to notice the Storyteller's hand behind such tailored powers). Other times, the players will have a trully &quot;winner&quot; build, unless you tailor everithing with such builds in mind-tailoring the enemy to the characters and the situation seems similar to &quot;narrative powers&quot;, just more dependant on luck, unless you state that the discipline doesn't need to roll in order to activate, in which case it would be merely an &quot;I Win&quot; button.<br /> <br /> Many gamers find such problems (or such adversarial storytelling) distasteful. The &quot;narrative&quot; style was invented, among other things, with the idea of eliminating the need of said arms race, by stating that not all things happen because of dice, that some events are just a deus ex machina and some characters are beyond normal rules.<br /> <br /> WoD was created with this concept (&quot;narrative power&quot;) in mind. It's both part of the rules and part of the setting. Of course, anyone can &quot;golden rule&quot; it away, as with anything else (albeit it might require some extra paperwork).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-07-2015, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T17:39:40-08:00","id":781969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781946#post781946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that such method may lead to problems with powergaming. For a thing, it <i>seems</i> to reward powergaming. 15 points in everything isn't really very impressive from a powergamer point of view, giving the <i>impression </i>that you can defeat anything with a strong fighter. (Really, 15 in everything it's still pretty weak. The avatar of Fenris, a mere fragment of a mere Incarna, has 20 in Rage. 100-1000 seems more appropriate for the really big things, the destroyer of worlds shouldn't die by falling a very tall cliff).<br /> <br /> I think that style leads the storyteller to situations in which, because of the skill of the players building killer machines, he will have to start creating Disciplines (or other powers) like this one...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...in order to prevent characters from slaying everything, starting an &amp;quot;arms race&amp;quot; with his players that he will likely win...most of the time...(after all, giving an Antediluvian a &amp;quot;surprise&amp;quot; Discipline that he hadn't five minutes earlier equals denying his defeat by narrative means...which his players might find injust, where they to notice the Storyteller's hand behind such tailored powers). Other times, the players will have a trully &amp;quot;winner&amp;quot; build, unless you tailor everithing with such builds in mind-tailoring the enemy to the characters and the situation seems similar to &amp;quot;narrative powers&amp;quot;, just more dependant on luck, unless you state that the discipline doesn't need to roll in order to activate, in which case it would be merely an &amp;quot;I Win&amp;quot; button.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry a few things to clarify.<br /> <br /> I can't really afford much outside the core rulebooks, and don't even own all of them. Therefore 'creature X' isn't a good comparison to give me, as I'll never give it.<br /> <br /> I prefer to express power through powers. However, the only way a creature will have a power it didn't have 5 minutes ago is if the session has only been going on for two minutes. I don't like to give powers during a game, so if I forgot to give immunity to nuclear weapons and my players get their hands on nuclear weapons, then byebye monster, that anti-stick power was worthless.<br /> <br /> I am also lucky enough not to play with minmaxers, but if I did I'd bump the minimum stay for superpowerful beings up (so instead of gigantic spirits having minimum Rage 15 Gnosis 15 Willpower 15 it might be closer to 40, I don't know). But it's not the only way to increase power.<br /> <br /> I've also let PC victories stand when the setting says they shouldn't. Why? Because I find it fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WoD was created with this concept (&amp;quot;narrative power&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> in mind. It's both part of the rules and part of the setting. </div> </div> </div>Cool, so where's all the narrative mechanics? I see the use of scenes as a measure of time....and that's it. The rest is pretty solidly simulationist. There are games that bake the idea of narrative power into their games, both Mutants and Masterminds and Fate give systems for players and GMs to influence the story. There's games which use failing forwards or sideways, games based on building the plot. These are the games built around narrative power.<br /> <br /> Oh, wait, I forgot, only the 'Storyteller' is allowed narrative power. I have to sit here while his story unfolds because this is a 'narrative' game where the 'story' matters. Where some things players just can't affect. And the 'Storyteller' always bans me from making choo choo noises.<br /> <br /> Facd it, there are big differences between encouraging narrative play and encouraging railroading. I'd rather have players able to spend a Fate Point and go 'I just so happened to pack Garlic' than be encouraged to go 'Samuel McAweome the Haight must survive at all costs so the story works' because the former is a narrative mechanic, the latter is railroading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T18:18:41-08:00","id":781989,"title":"","content":"And I think that's cool, but also understand why the orthodox might complain.<br /> <br /> About the &quot;Narrative Mechanic&quot;. The very concept of such it's anathema, because any mechanic can be abused by its technicians <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . WoD was created with the absolute and undisputed power of the Storyteller in mind. You can use to set your players free, to chain them, or to have a middle ground (say, by tailoring Ur-Shulgi to the players. If the players are expected to have Time Stop magic, <i>Of Course</i> that Ur-Shulgi has created a ritual that protects against that. You are protected by the fact that the guy hasn't a &quot;normal&quot; character sheet, until you give him one).<br /> <br /> Of course that the players haven't solid rules (that they could abuse) to give them &quot;Narrative Powers&quot;. If the Storyteller wants, he can give an Artifact or something to &quot;empower&quot; the players into doing the impossible. The Storyteller has many tools to make any sort of number crunching useless. I think than that's the point (because I've read such reasoning in many of the books. It may be a wrong reasoning, of course.)<br /> <br /> And all of this isn't to weaken the simulationism:<br /> <br /> Helios it's the supreme spirit of the Sun, necessary for it's existence, and the basic book of Werewolf states that destroying Helios should be as difficult as destroying the actual Sun, if not more.<br /> <br /> How many &quot;life points&quot; has the Sun?, how big has to be your stick to destroy it?.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> THAT might explain why the ortodox might find more than a little wierd to defeat such a power with the &quot;average&quot; damage that can be caused by a furry, or by a guy with Strength 10 or so. If you preffer to make spirits much weaker than that, it's OK (specially in Demon, that it's a different game, with different asumptions) For Werewolf, however, it's more unorthodox than playing a Salubri with three heads. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-07-2015, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T20:18:07-08:00","id":782051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781989#post781989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think that's cool, but also understand why the orthodox might complain.<br /> <br /> About the &quot;Narrative Mechanic&quot;. The very concept of such it's anathema, because any mechanic can be abused by its technicians <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . WoD was created with the absolute and undisputed power of the Storyteller in mind. You can use to set your players free, to chain them, or to have a middle ground (say, by tailoring Ur-Shulgi to the players. If the players are expected to have Time Stop magic, <i>Of Course</i> that Ur-Shulgi has created a ritual that protects against that. You are protected by the fact that the guy hasn't a &quot;normal&quot; character sheet, until you give him one).<br /> <br /> Of course that the players haven't solid rules (that they could abuse) to give them &quot;Narrative Powers&quot;. If the Storyteller wants, he can give an Artifact or something to &quot;empower&quot; the players into doing the impossible. The Storyteller has many tools to make any sort of number crunching useless. I think than that's the point (because I've read such reasoning in many of the books. It may be a wrong reasoning, of course.)<br /> <br /> And all of this isn't to weaken the simulationism:<br /> <br /> Helios it's the supreme spirit of the Sun, necessary for it's existence, and the basic book of Werewolf states that destroying Helios should be as difficult as destroying the actual Sun, if not more.<br /> <br /> How many &quot;life points&quot; has the Sun?, how big has to be your stick to destroy it?.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> THAT might explain why the ortodox might find more than a little wierd to defeat such a power with the &quot;average&quot; damage that can be caused by a furry, or by a guy with Strength 10 or so. If you preffer to make spirits much weaker than that, it's OK (specially in Demon, that it's a different game, with different asumptions) For Werewolf, however, it's more unorthodox than playing a Salubri with three heads. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always took the &quot;(Blank celestines existence is necessary for (blank) physical objects existence&quot; with a grain of salt. Sure destroying luna may be as hard as destroying the actual moon, sure destroying her may collapse the entire &quot;lunar realm, sure it may alter the flow of prime around the moon so much it becomes a &quot;no magic&quot; zone, but I don't believe the rock floating in the sky somehow needs a cosmic caretaker to survive. That's like saying if a random spirit attached itself to the concept of harry potter and died, then harry potter would have never existed(and yes I do realize the &quot;In a universe with magic..&quot; arguement, but we don't have cosmic caretakers in RL so why are they necessary somewhere that functions nearly the same?)<br /> <br /> then again I personally believe that celestines and above are just spirits that are so powerful they've become a spirit &quot;Realms&quot; of sorts(the wyrm Is malfeas, Gaia Is the penumbra, etc.) and celestines are just in the process of turning(like a tree thats roots reach deep into the ground, making it unable to move, but hasn't yet truely become a &quot;part&quot; of it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T21:17:29-08:00","id":782069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=782051#post782051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I always took the &quot;(Blank celestines existence is necessary for (blank) physical objects existence&quot; with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? It was mentioned out of character. It's like assuming that BattleTech was just kidding about using stompy robots as the superior vehicular combat unit, in spite of substantial mechanical and narrative focus supporting this as a fact within the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure destroying luna may be as hard as destroying the actual moon, sure destroying her may collapse the entire &quot;lunar realm, sure it may alter the flow of prime around the moon so much it becomes a &quot;no magic&quot; zone, but I don't believe the rock floating in the sky somehow needs a cosmic caretaker to survive. </div> </div> </div>In Werewolf, it does. In another out of character explanation, it details how spirits can survive the destruction of their representation in the physical world, but if you kill the spirit, that thing rapidly degrades and ends up destroyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's like saying if a random spirit attached itself to the concept of harry potter and died, then harry potter would have never existed(and yes I do realize the &quot;In a universe with magic..&quot; arguement, but we don't have cosmic caretakers in RL so why are they necessary somewhere that functions nearly the same?) </div> </div> </div>Spirits don't get randomly attached as an assignment like in Exalted. They arise from whatever they might, and they're not caretakers so much as the vital essence of that thing's existence. Again, the setting assumes that animism is how things work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> then again I personally believe that celestines and above are just spirits that are so powerful they've become a spirit &quot;Realms&quot; of sorts(the wyrm Is malfeas, Gaia Is the penumbra, etc.) and celestines are just in the process of turning(like a tree thats roots reach deep into the ground, making it unable to move, but hasn't yet truely become a &quot;part&quot; of it.) </div> </div> </div>You could do that, but it's not really supported by the setup provided in the books. Also, the members of the Triat are Supernals, which are above Celestines. Gaia is also above Celestine status with the basic assumption being &quot;above Supernals&quot;, though some Fera disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T22:02:21-08:00","id":782080,"title":"","content":"That the Triat it's above Celestines, it's defended even in Mage cosmology...it's one of the rare constants in WoD. It's said that Incarnas can become Celestines (albeit it's very rare), but nothing that I know points that a Celestine could grow to be like the Triat.<br /> <br /> But, even if the exact importance and power of the spirits can vary between settings (in Werewolf, they're<i> very </i>important) , I think that almost anyone, thinking with the framework of any line, can agree that trying to defeat the Wyrm in order to nullify the threat of Pentex it's like trying to move the sun because its light is hitting you in the eyes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T00:58:57-08:00","id":782136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781989#post781989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think that's cool, but also understand why the orthodox might complain.<br /> <br /> About the &amp;quot;Narrative Mechanic&amp;quot;. The very concept of such it's anathema, because any mechanic can be abused by its technicians <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . WoD was created with the absolute and undisputed power of the Storyteller in mind. You can use to set your players free, to chain them, or to have a middle ground (say, by tailoring Ur-Shulgi to the players. If the players are expected to have Time Stop magic, <i>Of Course</i> that Ur-Shulgi has created a ritual that protects against that. You are protected by the fact that the guy hasn't a &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; character sheet, until you give him one).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're saying the game gives you the right to railroad? Wow, it's not like any other system has that. Except that both M&amp;M and Fate have mechanics that allow for low level railroading, with the idea that you'll give them a Hero Point or Fate Point as compensation (in Fate you can refuse the Fate Point, but that game really empowers the players). Railroading isn't something that began with the cWoD, and it isn't unique to it. cWoD is a simulationist game that just reminds you to consider the story. I lose nothing by converting it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course that the players haven't solid rules (that they could abuse) to give them &amp;quot;Narrative Powers&amp;quot;. If the Storyteller wants, he can give an Artifact or something to &amp;quot;empower&amp;quot; the players into doing the impossible. The Storyteller has many tools to make any sort of number crunching useless. I think than that's the point (because I've read such reasoning in many of the books. It may be a wrong reasoning, of course.) </div> </div> </div>I don't want that, I want a game where the players aren't encouraged to go along with my plot, but where they are empowered to help create the plot. Otherwise you end up with the Haight problem and railroading (choo choo!) instead of narrative play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And all of this isn't to weaken the simulationism:<br /> <br /> Helios it's the supreme spirit of the Sun, necessary for it's existence, and the basic book of Werewolf states that destroying Helios should be as difficult as destroying the actual Sun, if not more.<br /> <br /> How many &amp;quot;life points&amp;quot; has the Sun?, how big has to be your stick to destroy it?.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Several thousand health levels, along with a power that makes it basically intangible and that within radius X things take damage just from being there. How easy is it to destroy the sun when your stick just melts away?<br /> <br /> But then players start adding heat shields to their sticks so they last just long enough to hit Helios. Let's hope they can survive his counterattacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THAT might explain why the ortodox might find more than a little wierd to defeat such a power with the &amp;quot;average&amp;quot; damage that can be caused by a furry, or by a guy with Strength 10 or so. If you preffer to make spirits much weaker than that, it's OK (specially in Demon, that it's a different game, with different asumptions) For Werewolf, however, it's more unorthodox than playing a Salubri with three heads. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>The problem I'm having is the massive amounts of 'wrongbadfun' that was said to me. I have no problems with people using stateless entities, I just wanted to give my take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T03:18:14-08:00","id":782187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=781902#post781902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. Spoken like somebody who has never turned up to run a game with a starting scenario and a folder of NPCs.<br /> <br /> I need to reorder my NPCs folder...<br /> <br /> My point that I have a completely different STing style to you. Maybe you like to plot out everything in advance, I like to throw caution to the winds and improvise a story, because it's fun. I did try to imply that I either let players have a chance to work it out before hand or to be able to win by exploiting everything at their disposal, but then again I hate invincible monsters, even in my novels (the closest I've gotten is a monster likely to ignore damage due to their biology. So a monster might be really powerful, but if the PCs are facing it they have at least a slim chance of winning.]<br /> <br /> If they win they haven't 'derailed the plot', they've 'taken the story in a new direction'. Frankly the use of the word 'derail' implies a lot to me, but that might be because my games are very loosely plotted.</div> </div> </div> </div>WTF dude. In which part does something being too strong for the PC's construe as railroading? If a thing is conceptually too big to fight, there is no point in giving it stats on the same level as the PC's. That does not mean that you are railroading anything. It means that people need to be clever about solving things. Putting narrative threads that are supposed to be scenery and backstory into simplistic mechanics meant for base conflict resolution hasn't ever helped anything. Just see D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> And I'm quite proud of the fact that I do not stat out the NPCs or bother with making them in advance. I have their agendas and style and let them roll and see what they end up doing in reaction the the PC's. Just like what I plot is openended enough that I never really go where they will go.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:35:54-08:00","id":782293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=782069#post782069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Spirits don't get randomly attached as an assignment like in Exalted. They arise from whatever they might, and they're not caretakers so much as the vital essence of that thing's existence. Again, the setting assumes that animism is how things work.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well exalted was originally hinted at being a precursor to the modern cWOD....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=782069#post782069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do that, but it's not really supported by the setup provided in the books. Also, the members of the Triat are Supernals, which are above Celestines. Gaia is also above Celestine status with the basic assumption being &quot;above Supernals&quot;, though some Fera disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, That's why I gave the example of Gaia being the penumbra. Supernals are beings that completed the transfer to spirit realm in my runs. Celestines like luna are simply stuck to their physical object like a tree to the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:50:05-08:00","id":782298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=782293#post782293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well exalted was originally hinted at being a precursor to the modern cWOD....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>For one book. And that got scrapped between the writing and printing, leading to the modern arrangement of &quot;make a lot of easter egg references and re-use names, but nothing more.&quot; In any case, Werewolf cosmology is emphatically not Exalted cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T08:18:23-08:00","id":782311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=782298#post782298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For one book. And that got scrapped between the writing and printing, leading to the modern arrangement of &quot;make a lot of easter egg references and re-use names, but nothing more.&quot; In any case, Werewolf cosmology is emphatically not Exalted cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant that it's mostly up to storyteller opinion. There are very few &quot;definites&quot; in WOD, just unpopular opinions and anyone who says another's play-style is wrong just because it doesn't conform to the majority opinion is narrow minded(to put it politely).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T12:01:34-08:00","id":782420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778610-fallen-vs-pentex?p=782187#post782187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WTF dude. In which part does something being too strong for the PC's construe as railroading? If a thing is conceptually too big to fight, there is no point in giving it stats on the same level as the PC's. That does not mean that you are railroading anything. It means that people need to be clever about solving things. Putting narrative threads that are supposed to be scenery and backstory into simplistic mechanics meant for base conflict resolution hasn't ever helped anything. Just see D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, a few things.<br /> <br /> One, I did not say something being too strong for the PCs is inherently railroading. In my later posts I do say that 'total Storyteller empowerment' is an inherent licence to railroad (or at least try to), but I never think a monster being unbeatable is railroading, I just don't like to represent it as statless.<br /> <br /> Also, have you ever played Fate? It is a game where the mechanics support building a story, significantly more than cWoD's do (again, not a bash at cWoD), as players get bonuses from being forced to follow the storyline (in the form of Fate Points) and have a mechanic for players to directly affect the story (in the form of Fate Points). Simple, but not simplistic mechanics, although they might not be your thing if you don't like player empowerment.<br /> <br /> I haven't played D&amp;D in over 2 years. I don't even like it, and never brought it up support me because it doesn't, I instead mentioned M&amp;M and Fate, mainly Fate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I'm quite proud of the fact that I do not stat out the NPCs or bother with making them in advance. I have their agendas and style and let them roll and see what they end up doing in reaction the the PC's. Just like what I plot is openended enough that I never really go where they will go. </div> </div> </div>Cool, it sounds like an awesome game. I however do need the stats, or else I feel like I'm railroading. It's entirely a personal thing, I've seen really good not railroaded games without stated in advance NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T01:17:48-08:00","id":782682,"title":"","content":"Fate is cool. It's not for every style of game, but it's loads of fun. Especially the character generation. Even in Fate you can judge that the characters cannot reasonably affect somethign without plot, though. It actually reinforces the concept of you needing to generate appropriate aspects to do what you want to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T03:10:32-08:00","id":782714,"title":"","content":"I agree with Fate, poor aspects can make it horrible to play because you can't affect anything. However, it makes it simple to make something unbeatable but still usable like a character: give it a skill or more at 5 over the game's skill cap (so +9 in a standard starting game). I agree it's not for everything, cWoD just wouldn't work anymore without loads of crunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}